<div class="modal fade" id="discordModal" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="discordModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog modal-dialog-centered modal-lg">
      <div class="modal-content">
        <div class="modal-header">
          <h1 class="modal-title fs-5" id="discordModalLabel">Configure Discord Webhooks</h1>
          <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button>
        </div>
        <div class="modal-body">
            <p>Discord has become a popular platform for creating event communities, by using Discord Webhooks we can automatically share your event adverts to your discord server.</p>
            <h3>Channel Integrations</h3>
            <p>To allow us to share your events, pick the channel you want us to share to and select the edit option, and head to the section labeled <b>Integrations</b>.</p>
            <p>You should see a Webhooks section, with a Create Webhook button.</p>
            <div class="d-flex">
              <div>
                <div class="bg-secondary px-3 pt-3 pb-1 rounded text-white mb-3 d-flex gap-4">
                  <img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dapc3dsxv/image/upload/c_scale,w_150/lrpEvents/LRPTicketsSkewedBlue15k_ukn44a.png"  />
                  <div>
                    <p>When creating the Webhook we ask that you use this image, and the name 'LRPTickets.co.uk'.</p>
                    <p>We want our users, and your attendees to have confidence in where the post has come from and this little bit of branding goes a long way in doing that.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p>Use the Copy Webhook URL button, and save your webhook integration.</p>  
              </div>
              
            </div>
            <p>Now come back to LRP Tickets, and paste your webhook url here, and save your details. Now when you edit an event and mark it ready for advertising it will automatically share to discord.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="modal-footer">
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Close</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
</div>